        <section class="docs-section" id="editor" aria-labelledby="editor-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="docs-eyebrow">Guide</p>
            <h2 id="editor-title">Edit and export recordings</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="guide-stack">
            <article>
              <h3>Open and review</h3>
              <p>
                After a standard video recording stops, Luxel opens the editor with a
                preview, source filename, duration, dimensions, audio status, alpha status,
                estimated file size, Save Original, and Export controls.
              </p>
              <p>
                Rename the source file in place, move to newer or older recordings in the
                same folder, or open an existing media file with <code>luxel editor &lt;file&gt;</code>.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Trim, resize, and retime</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Use Timeline start and end controls to trim the output range.</li>
                <li>Choose Original, percentage size presets, or Custom width and height.</li>
                <li>Use Crop to Fill when fitting the output size.</li>
                <li>Set frame rate and playback speed from 0.1x to 10x.</li>
                <li>Preview playback loops inside the trim range.</li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Choose export formats</h3>
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Format</th>
                    <th>Notes</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td>MP4 (H.264)</td>
                    <td>Most-compatible Apple-native video export with Compact, Balanced, or High quality.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>MP4 (HEVC)</td>
                    <td>Smaller-file HEVC export with Compact, Balanced, or High quality.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>MOV (ProRes 422)</td>
                    <td>Apple-native editing/master export with fixed High quality and LPCM audio.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>MOV (ProRes 4444)</td>
                    <td>Apple-native high-fidelity ProRes export with fixed High quality and LPCM audio.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>GIF</td>
                    <td>Animated image export. Audio is dropped. Supports loop and dithering options.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>APNG</td>
                    <td>Lossless animated PNG export. Audio is dropped.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>WebM (VP9)</td>
                    <td>Registered external codec export with Compact, Balanced, or High quality.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
              <p class="tip">
                The format menu can select multiple formats and shows size estimates when
                Luxel can calculate them. MP4, MOV, and WebM exports use even pixel dimensions.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Adjust audio</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Use Include Audio to mute or keep audio for formats that support it.</li>
                <li>Set audio level from 0% to 200%.</li>
                <li>Enable Normalize Audio to smooth loudness during export.</li>
                <li>Audio-only sources export as M4A, ALAC M4A, WAV, CAF, or FLAC.</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="tip">GIF and APNG always drop audio.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Export actions</h3>
              <p>
                During export, Luxel shows progress and lets you cancel. After export,
                actions include Open, Reveal in Finder, Save a Copy, Open With, Copy File,
                Copy Path, and Share. Multi-format export creates a batch folder named
                after the source recording.
              </p>
              <p class="tip">
                Copy Frame and Save Frame As use the current paused frame and save PNG output.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section" id="transcripts" aria-labelledby="transcripts-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="docs-eyebrow">Guide</p>
            <h2 id="transcripts-title">Create local transcripts</h2>
            <p>
              Luxel uses local Apple Speech transcription for recordings with audio. Use
              the editor for review workflows or the CLI when you need transcript files
              in scripts.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="split-grid">
            <article>
              <h3>In the editor</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Open a recording with audio in the editor.</li>
                <li>Use the transcript preview to generate or review transcript text.</li>
                <li>Search transcript text or select transcript spans to jump playback.</li>
                <li>Leave Segment Transcript Turns enabled for Apple Intelligence turn grouping.</li>
                <li>Turn it off in Settings > Output for faster raw transcripts on long recordings.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>From the command line</h3>
              <pre><code>luxel transcribe demo.m4a &gt; demo.txt
luxel transcribe demo.mp4 --output demo.json --json --overwrite
luxel transcribe demo.mp4 --locale en_US --semantic-turns</code></pre>
              <p class="tip">
                Plain text is printed to stdout by default. Use <code>--json</code> for
                full turn-segmented transcript data.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section" id="workflows" aria-labelledby="workflows-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="docs-eyebrow">Workflows</p>
            <h2 id="workflows-title">Compound workflows</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="workflow-grid">
            <article>
              <h3>Capture, refine, export, share</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Record a display, window, or area.</li>
                <li>Stop to open the editor.</li>
                <li>Trim the range, choose size, frame rate, and speed.</li>
                <li>Export as MP4, HEVC, ProRes MOV, GIF, APNG, or WebM.</li>
                <li>Use Copy Path, Share, or Reveal in Finder from the exported file menu.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Fast GIF from a selected area</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Create an export preset with GIF format and the desired destination.</li>
                <li>Set it as the Quick Recording preset.</li>
                <li>
                  Open Area, draw a selection, and press
                  <span class="shortcut-keys shortcut-keys--inline" aria-label="Option-click">
                    <kbd class="is-modifier" title="Option">⌥</kbd>
                    <kbd class="is-word" title="Click">click</kbd>
                  </span>
                  Record.
                </li>
                <li>Let the preset run its post-action after capture.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Repeat a previous capture</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Turn on Remember Last Capture in Presets settings.</li>
                <li>Make a normal capture once.</li>
                <li>Use Quick Record Last from the shortcut, CLI, URL automation, or App Shortcut.</li>
                <li>For a new selected area, use the area picker's Quick Record action with the active quick preset.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Replay a bug after it happens</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Enable Replay Buffer before the session starts.</li>
                <li>Choose a 1 minute, 2 minute, or 5 minute length based on how much history you need.</li>
                <li>When the issue appears, click Export or run <code>luxel clip --seconds 30 --wait</code>.</li>
                <li>Open the clip in the editor or let the quick export destination handle it.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Paused-frame handoff</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Open a recording in the editor.</li>
                <li>Pause on the frame you need.</li>
                <li>Use Copy Frame or Save Frame As from the editor actions.</li>
                <li>Use the saved PNG or clipboard image in the destination app.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Scripted export and transcript</h3>
              <ol>
                <li>Install the command from Settings > Command Line.</li>
                <li>Run <code>luxel convert demo.mp4 demo.webm --width 1280 --height 720</code>.</li>
                <li>Run <code>luxel transcribe demo.mp4 --output demo.txt</code>.</li>
                <li>Use <code>--json</code> when another tool needs structured output.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

